Actually, let me reconsider. The issue is a heap-buffer-overflow READ 4. Let me look at the format 12/13 `CmapSubtableLongSegmented::collect_unicodes`:

```cpp
inline void collect_unicodes (hb_set_t *out) const
{
  for (unsigned int i = 0; i < this->groups.len; i++) {
    out->add_range (this->groups[i].startCharCode,
                    MIN ((hb_codepoint_t) this->groups[i].endCharCode,
                         (hb_codepoint_t) HB_UNICODE_MAX));
  }
}
```

This reads `groups[i].startCharCode` and `groups[i].endCharCode` which are HBUINT32 (4 bytes). If `groups.len` is larger than the actual array, this would be a READ 4 out of bounds.

